            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Dramatically. As a rule of thumb, cure rate roughly halves for every 18 degree drop in temperature, so an epoxy that walks on in 24 hours at 70 degrees may need 48 hours at 50 degrees and may never cure properly below its minimum application temperature. What matters is slab temperature, not air temperature.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why is my epoxy floor still tacky?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
