            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Warm the space and keep air moving. Bringing the garage to a stable 75 to 80 degrees with a heater and a fan meaningfully shortens cure, and a dehumidifier helps in humid weather. Never point a direct flame heater at a curing floor, and never add solvent to thin the mix — both cause more problems than they solve.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long before you can wash a new epoxy floor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Wait until full chemical cure, typically seven days minimum and up to 30 for some systems. Water and cleaners on a partially cured film can leave permanent haze or soft spots. Dust mop as needed in the meantime and keep any wet cleaning off the floor until the manufacturer's cure period has passed.",
          },
        },
      ],
