        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Garage floor epoxy drying time</strong> at 70 degrees runs roughly: tack free in half a day, walkable overnight, furniture at three days, and a car at five to seven. Full cure keeps going for a week to a month, and that is when wet cleaning and salt exposure become safe.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Every one of those numbers is written for a 70-degree slab. <strong class="text-white">Measure the concrete, not the air</strong>, add days when it is cold, hit the recoat window on the data sheet, and keep the car in the driveway an extra two days. Nothing about a coating rewards impatience.
          </p>
        </div>
